<title>POLAND: Polish BOS extends loss in profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Polish BOS extends loss in profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Ochrony Srodowiska (BOS) extended Tuesday's loss, falling 5.4 percent to 43.5 zlotys in profit-taking after its debut on Monday well above its issue price of 29 zlotys, traders said.</p>
<p>BOS traded in moderate 5.8-million-zloty turnover.</p>
<p>&quot;No wonder why many want to take profits after the bank's debut at 48 zlotys,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Some said BOS was likely to extend losses in the next few sessions but saw it rebounding later to about 50 zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
